      "text": "To determine the area of the shaded regions in Wei's logo, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the side length of the square**: Wei has designed a logo that is 20 inches on each side. \n   \\[\n   \\text{Side length of the square} = 20 \\text{ inches}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the radius of each circle**: Each circle is tangent to two sides of the square and its two adjacent circles. This means the circles are arranged such that they form a smaller concentric square inside the larger square. The diameter of each circle is equal to the side length of the smaller square formed by the centers of the circles. Since each circle is tangent to two adjacent circles and two sides of the square, the distance from the center of each circle to the side of the square is half the side length of the larger square, which is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{20}{2} = 10 \\text{ inches}\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the radius \\( r \\) of each circle is:\n   \\[\n   r = \\frac{10}{2} = 5 \\text{ inches}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the area of the circle**: The area \\( A \\) of a circle is given by the formula:\n   \\[\n   A = \\pi r^2\n   \\]\n   Substituting the radius \\( r = 5 \\):\n   \\[\n   A = \\pi (5)^2 = 25\\pi \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total area of the four circles**: Since there are four circles, the total area \\( A_{\\text{total}} \\) of the four circles is:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{total}} = 4 \\times 25\\pi = 100\\pi \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the area of the shaded regions**: The area of the shaded regions is the area of the entire square minus the area of the four circles:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{shaded}} = \\text{Area of the square} - \\text{Total area of the four circles}\n   \\]\n   The area of the square with side length 20 inches is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of the square} = 20^2 = 400 \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the area of the shaded regions is:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{shaded}} = 400 - 100\\pi\